  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Employment and Entrepreneurship (E&amp;E) activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Rwanda):  .The Employment and.Entrepreneurship (E&amp;E) activity will use FY 2022 funds to address the.problem of insufficient employment opportunities and limited entrepreneurship.success for Rwandans. E&amp;E will build the capacity of Rwandans, in.particular women, youth, and persons with disabilities, in key technical and.soft skills to participate in the workforce (focusing on opportunities in.agriculture) and to establish and grow inclusive enterprises. E&amp;E will use.facilitative, demand-driven, private-sector-led approaches to developing.economic opportunities at scale. The activity will work with relevant actors in.generating employment and entrepreneurship opportunities. Interventions will.include rural, urban, and peri-urban areas within the Feed the Future zone of.influence, 13 rural districts out of 30, and in Kigali, given its importance as.the nation&apos;s commercial hub. . .$1.6 million within this activity contributes to meeting the &quot;Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprises (MSME)&quot; earmark of $9.6 million. Additionally, the activity is allocating $200,000 to promote gender equality and women empowerment initiatives, through the Gender Equity and Equality Action (GEEA) Fund. The activity most closely aligns to GEEA Priority 1: Promote Economic Competitiveness through Well-Paying, Quality Jobs.. .E&amp;E contributes to USAID&apos;s Country Development Cooperation Strategy Objective 3, &quot;Increase Inclusive and Sustainable Private Sector Driven Growth&quot; and to USAID&apos;s Global Food Security Strategy. ...........</narrative>
  </description>
